   fixed a zeropage hit when sorting with device column.
   enabled context menus in device list (rename disabled for now as it's not really functional).
   pressing middle button outside of a lister just disables inline renaming. (fab1)
 - windowclass.c
   made window_loaduri handle "" paths (device list), which removes yet another zeropage hit with
   back toolbar button. (fab1)
 - sysinfowinclass.c: removed buffer overflow formatting cache strings. (piru)
 - appclass.c, deficon_getpath.c, device_func.c, file_func.c, fonts.c,
   iconio.c, iconviewclass.c, listviewclass.c, listviewclass_nlist.c,
   movelist.c, shotcuts.c, wbstart.c, iconlib/diskobject.c, private.c:
   avoid peeking memory before passed pointer if string is "". (piru)
 - file_func.c: optimized is_path_contained(). (piru)
 - deficon_getpath.c: fixed deficon_getpath() not to overflow the passed
   buffer size. empty DefIcon_Path envvar is considered invalid and is
   replaced by ENVARC:sys/ now. (piru)
 - iconlib/diskobject.c: fixed getdeficon() not to overflow the passed
   buffer size. empty DefIcon_Path envvar is considered invalid and is
   replaced by ENVARC:sys/ now. (piru)
 - iconviewclass.c fixed MM_Notify_Change NOTIFYTAG_Monitor_Device_Name
   'if ( p[ len - 1 ] = ':' ) )' -bug. (piru)
 - prefs_advanced.c
   - on-the-fly changeable variables are now reset to default if deactivated
   - fixed memory leak in cleanup
   (tokai)
 - prefswin_listerclass.c
   Fixed underscore handling for mode gadget and added missing online
   help strings. (geit)
 - prefswin_icondisplayclass.c
   Fixed color gadget label to support underscore. (geit)
 - colormap.c: made faster & shorter with LoadRGB32(). (piru)
 - clickpathclass.c, clickpathbuttonclass.c, clipboard.c, makelinkwinclass.c, wbstart.c:
   Replaced strncpy() by stccpy(). (itix)
 - wbstartlib.c, soundlib.c:
   Replaced Remove() by REMOVE(). (itix)
 - appclass.c, devicelistclass.c, listviewclass.c, listviewlistclass.c, navigationclass.c,
   recog.c, rexx.c, viewgroupclass.c: replaced strncpy() by stccpy(), removed few dupe
   strlen() calls, changed Remove() to REMOVE(). (itix)
   Replaced Remove() by REMOVE().
 - contextmenu.c
   Added "create panel" to panel and panel item context menu. (geit)
 - capacity.c: shortened code by removed superfulous strncpy(). (itix)
 - fastcopy.c, findver.c, iconio.c, scandir.c, wbstartup.c: optimized threads a little by
   removing syncs where not needed. (itix)
 - infowinclass.c: fixed braindamaged stccpy() usage. (itix)
 - textviewclass.c
   fixed unwanted appending of text to view, when file gadget in clickpath was pressed. 
   (tokai)
 - iconclass.c/icondata.h/thumbs.c/deficonpool.c
   Smarter deficons support. Saves tons of memory. Faster. (kiero)
 - rexx.c: rewrote slightly. now fails if AMBIENT port already exists. also
   added code to rename the port (disabled). (piru)
 - iconclass.c/textbox.c
   labels for links are displayed in italics (same as in list).
   fixed label width calculations. (kiero)
 - path.c: avoid wrong behaviour if PATH_SIZE overflows. (piru)
 - listviewlistclass.c: avoid wrong behaviour if linkpath overflows. (piru)
 - deficonpool.c: avoid wrong behaviour if deficon_path overflows. (piru)
 - scandir.c: avoid wrong behaviour if icon path overflows. (piru)
 - clickpathclass.c, iconio.c, imagecache.c, imageviewclass.c, toolbarclass.c,
   windowclass.c: replaced strlen("string") with sizeof("string") - 1. (piru)
 - toolbarclass.c: fixed buffer overflow with "devices://" string alloc. (piru)
 - iconio.c: fixed buffer overflow with ".info" concatename. (piru)
 - findresultlistclass.c, imageviewclass.c, listviewclass.c, makedirwinclass.c,
   makelinkwinclass.c, mimetype.c, movefile.c, movelist.c, panelprefs.c,
   scandir.c: try to avoid buffer overflows when handling paths. (piru)
 - dosnotify.c/appclass.c/mimetype.c/prefs_advanced.c
   changed way dosnotify is handled for internal files. (kiero)
 - findclass.c: optimized code by reducing strlen() calls. (itix)
 - selectwinclass.c, recurse.c, makedirwinclass.c, imageviewclass.c: added more
   safety. (itix)
 - textviewclass.c: moved 6 (!!) strlen() calls outside of a loop. (piru)
 - findclass.c: why bother doing full strlen if you want to know if string
   has one or more chars? (piru)
 - dosnotify.c/dosnotify_start(): removed one strlen(). (itix)
 - listviewclass.c: removed couple of dupe strlen() calls, fixed few potential
   memory leaks. (itix)
 - notify.c/notify_action(): less strlen(). (itix)
 - toolbutton_historyclass.c: less strlen(). (itix)
 - viewgroupclass.c: even less strlen(), one inside two level loops. (piru)
 - distribution/filetypes/recognition.db
   14 new filetypes added (mostly archive formats and scripts) (tokai)
 - statusbarclass.c/setstatus(): cache strlen(). (itix)
 - name.c: name_build_info()/name_build_wintitle(): avoid peeking memory
   before passed pointer if string is "". (piru)
 - searchbarclass.c: less strlen(). (piru)
 - deficonpool.c
   function to get deficon name can poke return into given buffer. (kiero)
 - mimeuri.c: valid port range is 1 to 65535 inclusive, not 0 to 65534. (piru)
 - notify.c/notify_register(): fixed broken safety check, removed strlen(). (itix)
 - textviewclass.c
   avoid that small textfiles with only a few lines show up marked when reloaded 
   with clickpath gadget, also flickers less. (tokai)
 - devices.c: fixed some major braindamage in device_get_information. cures the
   bogus device used size metadata display. (piru)
 - mimetype.c: display 0 if getting device used size or total directory size
   fails. (piru)
 - devices.c/tr_devices_updateinfo(): sync in the end of loop for better safety. (itix)
 - getdirsize.c/tr_getdirsizes(): sync only once. (itix)
 - listviewclass.c/listview_createicon(): sync less often. (itix)

08.04.2006
 - panelbuttonclass.c, panelgroupclass.c: max panel size is set correctly now so that
   MUI doesnt make panel wider than a screen. My MorphOS icon is no longer draggable
   to panels. (itix)
 - panelgroupclass.c: fixed zipping which broke thanks to previous fix. (itix)
 - cpu.c, cpu.h: added some new cpu types. (piru)
 - altivec.c, altivec.h, cpu.c, gfx_alpha.c, gfx_scale.c, init.c,
   sysinfowinclass.c: added new use_altivec variable. has_altivec now has
   information about existance of altivec hw, while use_altivec tells if the
   altivec is to be used in Ambient. having no USE_ALTIVEC disables just
   use_altivec. (piru)
 - align_vec.c, align_vec.h: vec_ld_align is static inline now. (piru)

07.04.2006
 - iconclass.c: now finally respects snapshotted mymorphos window position and
   size. (itix)
 - iconviewclass.c: shortened and optimized code a little. (itix)
 - prefs_desktop.c: mymorphos window pos/size is now saved to the desktop prefs
   file. (itix)
 - appmessage.c
   fixed zeropage read if path was NULL (piru)
 - methodstack.c
   fixed zeropage read if methodstack_push_sync was called from
   main thread (piru)
 - listviewclass.c iconviewclass.c
   fixed zeropage hits in view_load_uri (fab1)
 - listviewclass.c typescanner.c
   Switched to new deficon system for listview icons. (fab1)

06.04.2006
 - prefswin_listerclass.c
   changed some labels and fixed underscore support for checkbox gadgets. (geit)
 - prefswin_windowclass.c
   added missing locale strings and renamed some labels. (geit)
 - columnslistclass.c
   added missing locale strings. (geit)
 - descparser.c debug.c debug.h menus.c
   - added DESCPARSER option to Debug menu for recognition and filetype parsing
   - besides enabling full debug with capslock on boot you can "setenv SAVE Ambient/all 1"
     which will do the same as long this var exists
   - it is now also possible to activate debug partitially by setting env
     vars (same Name as in Debug menu), e.g. "setenv SAVE Ambient/INIT 1" etc.
   (tokai)
 - panelgroupclass.c
   horizontal and symetrical panel background gradients are no longer repeated in all 
   buttons with MUI4 (tokai)
 - panelconfigwinclass.c
   detect MUI4 on the fly and use single popfrimage.mui instead popframe.mui and 
   popimage.mui if possible (no more USE_LEGACY required) (tokai)
 - prefswin_mainclass.c
   - frame and image clipboard is automatically used when MUI4 is detected
   - use proper frame for pages 
   (tokai)
 - clickpathclass.c: added compiler warning. (itix)
 - iconclass.c: now builds proper icon path and name automatically when the icon type is
   set to MV_Icon_Type_MyComputer. (itix)
 - iconviewclass.c: added checks for emptry MA_View_Path (""), MM_Rexx_Snapshot now
   snapshots "My MorphOS" window too. Snapshot dimensions are not respected still. (itix)
 - shortcuts.c: now only sets icon type for My MorphOS icon. (itix)
 - action.c debug.c debug.h descparser.c menus.c mimetype.c shortcuts.c
   - DESCPARSER debug class changed to more generic "MIMETYPE"
   - less serial debug noise on default 
   (tokai)
 - crawlclass.c/libs.c
   killed usage of muigfx.library as it's dead. (kiero)

05.04.2006
 - Makefile, Install
   create SYS:Prefs/Ambient/filetype sub directories according to mime
   specs (tokai)
 - recognition.db 
   added more than 60 matching rules (tokai)
 - prefs.c/h updatelist.c appclass.c prefswin_windowclass.c prefswin_listerclass.c columnslistclass.c/h
   listview*.c/h classes.c/h iconviewclass.c iconclass.c findresultlistclass.c viewgroupclass.c viewapi.c/h
   + Added settings for default window dimensions in prefs/window (applies to iconview and listview).
     Moved view arguments template to viewapi.h
   + Added settings for listviewclass : devices and files mode can be configured independently.
     Columns layout (order, sort mode, shown/hidden, icons size) can be set. Other specific options
     can also be set for each mode.
   + Added date&time, user, group columns for files mode. Added human readable size option too.
   + Added "display assigns" option for devices mode.
   + Listview class now uses the common cache system for its icons and thumbnails (each size is cached
     independently, using a different hash). 
   Please note that you may have to delete envarc:ambient.data and sys:prefs/ambient/ambient.prefs as
   some options could clash with previously saved ones (saved after 22.03.06). Sorry for that. (fab1)
 - thumbs.c
   Adjusted the generated hash to be the same as listview's one (for 64 pixels size), so that listview
   and iconview share the same cached images. (fab1)
 - gfx_pen.c
   Removed internal structures use. (fab1)
 - wbstart.c
   Apps without icon have their progdir in their homedir, not in ambient's homedir. (kiero)
 - appclass.c
   Check for LoadURI command without uri arg. (kiero)
 - cache.c
   Invalidating of entries did some not-completely-legal things with cache nodes. (kiero)
 - deficonpool.c/h
   Changed old, extension-based deficon system for new one, based on filetype. Devices use old
   system still. (kiero)
 - file_funct.c/h
   Removed isinfo(). duplicate from name.c. (kiero)
 - name.c/h
   Added name_truncateinfo/name_restoreinfo functions. (kiero)
 - findver.c/getdirsize.c/listviewclass.c
   Minor adjustments to new internals. (kiero)
 - iconclass.c/h
   Optimized image regeneration. Added _Refine attr. (kiero)
 - iconio.c/scandir.c/shortcuts.c
   Adjusted to new deficon scanner. Optimized memory allocations. (kiero)
 - iconviewclass.c
   Implemented new deficon scanner. (kiero)
 - mimetype.c
   Fixed merging of recognition.db types with user types. (kiero)
 - typescanner.c/threads.c
   Typescanner uses new deficon system. Optimized. Can generate thumnails if required. (kiero)
 - viewgroupclass.c
   String object was not disposed in some cases. (kiero)
 - config.h, mimetype.c
   USE_MIME_NOFALLBACKNAME, if used fallback "datatype" mimetype has no name and shows up
   empty. Helps when working on recognition.db (tokai)
 - mimetype.c mimeuri.h recog.c recog.h recognition.db
   - new recog command RECOGCMD_FINDSTRING: scans whole file for string occurence
   - cleaned up internal mimetypes definitions
   - try to detect os4 binaries properly by checking for __amigaos4__ symbol (not all
     OS4 bins can be detected that way yet). Other ELF binaries will be detected by 
     recognition.db later as they do not need special handling inside Ambient.
   (tokai)

   NOTE: to not slow down the yet unoptimized filytype scanning a temporary break for 
         RECOGCMD_AND was added (see #warning in recog.h), but it *doesnt* handle OR, BLOCKIN 
         and BLOCKOUT yet, so needs serious improvement. It should work fine with all current 
         rules in recognition.db though. :P (tokai)


03.04.2006
 - Makefile
